TITLE='Authentic title "Why Your First Million Feels Impossible (And The Next Comes Fast)" pairs a pain point with a reassuring compounding payoff. The script delivers the compounding-milestone math (9/6/4/3 years) plus psychology, debt and systems. The title\'s "next comes fast" is supported only with no withdrawals and steady 8% returns, and the opening "about three years" contradicts the video\'s own 9-year figure. STRONG against the cohort (borderline, about 2.08x). Association only.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background. Left: the recurring cartoon man (glasses, white T-shirt) holding a green piggy bank stands on a cliff edge; a curved black arrow points across a gap to a stack of banded cash on the opposite cliff. Heavy black three-line headline "THE FIRST $1,000,000 IS ALSO A B*$£€" (a censored-profanity "bitch" joke). At 320x180 the headline, $1,000,000 and the gap metaphor stay legible. Matches the title\'s difficulty framing; the profanity tease adds curiosity. It does not show the "next comes fast" payoff.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator motivational explainer: social-media comparison hook; claim that later millions come in ~3 years; channel pitch; why the first million is hard (learning, mistakes, fear, low risk tolerance); millionaires\' risk cushion; good vs bad debt; access to capital and opportunities; contributions vs compounding ($5,000 saved vs $80,000 growth); milestone timing (9/6/4/3 years); mindset shift; assets vs liabilities; tax incentives; systems over goals; emotions; 8% vs 10% returns; time as ally; pattern recognition; exclusive investments; start early ($300 at 25 vs $1,000 at 45); growth at $2-4M; financial vertigo; close. Most arithmetic reproduces. Errors: the opening "second million in about three years" contradicts the 9-year math; 2->3M takes 5.3 years, not 6; "lower fees" for hedge funds/PE is wrong; "inflation becomes less relevant" is misleading. The stored ending is complete.'
